2026-11-07T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2473) 'Planner search: heuristics for the shortest plan
 # uuid: cb587afc-ea43-529e-8115-b395a016fbbb
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Prediscussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-07T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2473) 'the planner's backtracking search finds the shortest plan without an exhaustive scan.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2473) 'the planner's bound-raising search and the domains it solves.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2473) 'Can the planner find the shortest plan for 16 cubes without scanning every bound in turn?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2473) '`shortestOf` raises a bound on the number of actions until a plan reaches its goals, through a backtracking decomposition. That search is exhaustive at each bound, so the whole search is exponential: fine for the Sussman anomaly at six actions, too slow for 16 cubes.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2473) 'Run the blocks-world domain at 16 cubes under a wall-clock budget. A plan that returns within budget, at the same length an exhaustive search would find, passes.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2473) 'Add three heuristics to the bound-raising search, each kept only if it holds plan length unchanged while cutting search time:
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2473) '- A lower bound supplied by the domain (admissible, so the rising bound starts higher and prunes branches that cannot reach a shorter plan).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2473) '- Memoising failed (state, bound) pairs, so a branch already shown to fail at a bound is never re-explored at that bound.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2473) '- Ordering alternatives by a heuristic, so the search tries the branch most likely to reach the goal first, before the branches it would otherwise explore in declaration order. Each heuristic ships behind its own control: a planted domain that breaks admissibility, a planted stale memo entry, and a planted heuristic that always ranks last, each of which must make its gate fail.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2473  1 LINE
 Text:Written
